payload.prompt:
INTENT
Link-creation callers that present a recognised API key are throttled against that key's own per-minute quota instead of the shared per-IP budget, so trusted integrators get a higher creation allowance while every existing anonymous client keeps exactly today's per-IP behaviour.

DESIGN
{
  "configuration": [
    {
      "default": "./links.db",
      "name": "LINKS_DB_PATH",
      "purpose": "Filesystem path to the SQLite database file. This is the only name the service reads and the only name tests may set; DATABASE_PATH is not read."
    },
    {
      "default": "http://localhost:8000",
      "name": "LINKS_BASE_URL",
      "purpose": "Origin used to build the short_url field in POST /api/links responses. Trailing slash is stripped."
    },
    {
      "default": "7",
      "name": "LINKS_CODE_LENGTH",
      "purpose": "Number of base62 characters in a generated short code. Values outside 4..16 are logged and the default is used."
    },
    {
      "default": "5",
      "name": "LINKS_CODE_MAX_ATTEMPTS",
      "purpose": "Bounded number of insert attempts when a generated code collides with the UNIQUE constraint before the request fails with 503."
    },
    {
      "default": "31536000",
      "name": "LINKS_MAX_TTL_SECONDS",
      "purpose": "Upper bound accepted for expires_in_seconds on POST /api/links (one year)."
    },
    {
      "default": "true",
      "name": "LINKS_RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED",
      "purpose": "Master switch for the limiter middleware. Parsed case-insensitively; 'false','0','no','off' disable it. When disabled no bucket is consulted and no 429 is ever produced, including for per-key quotas."
    },
    {
      "default": "10",
      "name": "LINKS_RATE_LIMIT_MAX",
      "purpose": "Per-IP creation allowance for POST /api/links inside one window. Also the base for the redirect allowance."
    },
    {
      "default": "60",
      "name": "LINKS_RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_SECONDS",
      "purpose": "Sliding window length in seconds, shared by the per-IP creation bucket, the per-IP redirect bucket and every per-key bucket."
    },
    {
      "default": "100",
      "name": "LINKS_RATE_LIMIT_REDIRECT_MULTIPLIER",
      "purpose": "Multiplier applied to LINKS_RATE_LIMIT_MAX to obtain the per-IP allowance for GET /{code} and GET /api/links/{code}/stats. Unchanged by this work."
    },
    {
      "default": "",
      "name": "SHORTENER_API_KEYS",
      "purpose": "Comma-separated name:quota pairs, e.g. 'alpha:100,beta:20'. Each entry is trimmed of surrounding whitespace; empty entries are ignored; an entry whose quota is not a base-10 integer >= 1, whose name is empty, or that contains no ':' is logged (name and value redacted) and skipped. Unset or empty means no key is recognised and POST /api/links behaves exactly as today."
    },
    {
      "default": "INFO",
      "name": "LOG_LEVEL",
      "purpose": "Root log level. Even at DEBUG no code path emits an X-API-Key value or a SHORTENER_API_KEYS entry value."
    }
  ],
  "data_model": [
    {
      "fields": [
        {
          "constraints": "PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, internal only, never exposed in any response",
          "name": "id",
          "type": "INTEGER"
        },
        {
          "constraints": "NOT NULL, UNIQUE \u2014 this constraint is the sole enforcer of short-code uniqueness",
          "name": "code",
          "type": "TEXT"
        },
        {
          "constraints": "NOT NULL, 1..2048 chars, http/https only",
          "name": "url",
          "type": "TEXT"
        },
        {
          "constraints": "NOT NULL, RFC3339 UTC, defaults to insert time",
          "name": "created_at",
          "type": "TEXT"
        },
        {
          "constraints": "NULL allowed; NULL means never expires",
          "name": "expires_at",
          "type": "TEXT"
        }
      ],
      "indexes": [
        "UNIQUE index on links.code (implicit from the UNIQUE constraint) \u2014 the redirect hot path is a single equality lookup on code; without it every GET /{code} scans the table"
      ],
      "name": "links",
      "purpose": "One row per shortened URL. Schema is frozen: SCHEMA_STATEMENTS is unchanged by this work and PRAGMA table_info(links) must return exactly these columns."
    },
    {
      "fields": [
        {
          "constraints": "PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT",
          "name": "id",
          "type": "INTEGER"
        },
        {
          "constraints": "NOT NULL, FOREIGN KEY -> links(id)",
          "name": "link_id",
          "type": "INTEGER"
        },
        {
          "constraints": "NOT NULL, RFC3339 UTC",
          "name": "clicked_at",
          "type": "TEXT"
        }
      ],
      "indexes": [
        "Index on clicks.link_id \u2014 GET /api/links/{code}/stats runs COUNT(*) and MAX(clicked_at) filtered by link_id; without it stats scans the whole clicks table"
      ],
      "name": "clicks",
      "purpose": "One row per served redirect, aggregated by the stats route. Schema frozen; no new column and no new table is introduced by per-key limiting."
    },
    {
      "fields": [
        {
          "constraints": "dict key. Exactly one of three namespaced forms: 'post:key:' + hash, 'post:ip:' + hash, 'get:ip:' + hash. Namespacing guarantees a key bucket and an IP bucket can never alias.",
          "name": "bucket_id",
          "type": "str"
        },
        {
          "constraints": "hexdigest of blake2b(salt=per-boot secrets.token_bytes(16), data=utf8(api_key or client_host)), truncated to 32 hex chars. The raw key value is never stored.",
          "name": "hash",
          "type": "str"
        },
        {
          "constraints": "monotonic timestamps, pruned to the last LINKS_RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_SECONDS on every touch; length bounded by the bucket's allowance",
          "name": "hits",
          "type": "collections.deque[float]"
        },
        {
          "constraints": ">= 1. For 'post:key:' buckets it is the quota parsed from SHORTENER_API_KEYS for that key; for 'post:ip:' it is LINKS_RATE_LIMIT_MAX; for 'get:ip:' it is LINKS_RATE_LIMIT_MAX * LINKS_RATE_LIMIT_REDIRECT_MULTIPLIER",
          "name": "allowance",
          "type": "int"
        },
        {
          "constraints": "monotonic timestamp used by the existing eviction when the dict exceeds MAX_TRACKED_KEYS",
          "name": "last_seen",
          "type": "float"
        }
      ],
      "indexes": [
        "Python dict keyed by bucket_id \u2014 O(1) lookup on every request; no scan. Cardinality is bounded by MAX_TRACKED_KEYS (module constant, 10000) plus at most len(SHORTENER_API_KEYS) key buckets, because unrecognised keys never allocate a bucket of their own."
      ],
      "name": "RateLimiterState (in-process, app/ratelimit.py, not persisted)",
      "purpose": "Sliding-window counters held in a single dict guarded by the existing threading.Lock. Vanishes on restart; never written to SQLite, a file or a log."
    },
    {
      "fields": [
        {
          "constraints": "same per-boot salted blake2b digest used for bucket ids; the plaintext key name from the environment is discarded after hashing",
          "name": "key_hash",
          "type": "str"
        },
        {
          "constraints": ">= 1; entries with a non-integer, zero or negative quota, an empty name, or no ':' separator are skipped at parse time",
          "name": "quota",
          "type": "int"
        }
      ],
      "indexes": [
        "Python dict keyed by key_hash \u2014 one O(1) constant-shape lookup per POST /api/links; a miss is indistinguishable in behaviour and cost from an absent header"
      ],
      "name": "ApiKeyQuotas (in-process, built once at startup from SHORTENER_API_KEYS)",
      "purpose": "Frozen mapping from hashed key to quota, consulted by the middleware to decide whether a presented key is recognised."
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "choice": "Inside the existing RateLimitMiddleware (pure ASGI, added before routing), which inspects scope['method'], scope['path'] and the raw scope['headers'] list for x-api-key and returns a canned 429 JSON response itself.",
      "decision": "Where per-key throttling is enforced",
      "rationale": "A caller that blew its quota gets a 429 without the service parsing its body or opening a SQLite connection, so a flood of oversized or malformed POSTs costs almost nothing and can never leave a half-written links row.",
      "rejected": [
        "A FastAPI dependency on the create route: runs after routing and body parsing, so a malformed JSON body would produce 422 instead of 429 and would violate the 'no DB connection opened' criterion.",
        "A separate middleware class: duplicates window/eviction/lock logic and risks the two limiters disagreeing about the window boundary."
      ]
    },
    {
      "choice": "Only for POST /api/links: hash the header value with the per-boot salt, look it up in ApiKeyQuotas; on a hit use bucket 'post:key:'+hash with that key's quota, on a miss (or absent header) use 'post:ip:'+hash(client_host) with LINKS_RATE_LIMIT_MAX. Redirect and stats routes never read the header.",
      "decision": "How a presented API key selects a bucket",
      "rationale": "alpha exhausting 100 creations from one address leaves both beta and the anonymous per-IP budget untouched for that same address, and 1000 attacker-invented keys from one address behave exactly like 1000 key-less requests.",
      "rejected": [
        "Counting key-limited hits in the per-IP bucket as well: a trusted integrator's 100 allowed creations would immediately exhaust the 10-request IP budget for everyone behind that address.",
        "Allocating a bucket for every observed key value: unbounded memory growth driven by attacker-controlled input, defeating MAX_TRACKED_KEYS."
      ]
    },
    {
      "choice": "The environment value is parsed at startup into {blake2b(salt, name) -> quota} and the plaintext names are dropped; request header values are hashed on arrival and only the digest is used as a dict key. Parse failures log the entry index and the reason, never the text. No response, no DB column and no log record can contain a key.",
      "decision": "How key material is kept out of storage and logs",
      "rationale": "Grepping the sqlite files or DEBUG-level logs for 's3cret-alpha' after a full run finds nothing, so a leaked log bundle does not hand over integrator credentials.",
      "rejected": [
        "Storing the plaintext key as the dict key: it would appear in any repr/exception traceback of the limiter state.",
        "A static salt or a plain unsalted hash: identical digests across boots make an offline dictionary attack against short key names cheap."
      ]
    },
    {
      "choice": "Fail soft, exactly like the rest of app/config.py: split on ',', strip whitespace around the entry, the name and the quota, drop empty entries, require exactly one ':' with a non-empty name and a base-10 integer quota >= 1; anything else is logged at WARNING (redacted) and skipped. The process always starts.",
      "decision": "What happens to malformed SHORTENER_API_KEYS entries",
      "rationale": "A typo in one integrator's quota does not take the whole shortener down; that integrator simply falls back to the anonymous per-IP limit, which is the safe direction.",
      "rejected": [
        "Raising at startup: one bad character in an ops-managed env var causes a total outage.",
        "Treating quota 0 as 'block this key': introduces a denial path that looks like an auth decision and is indistinguishable to the caller from a normal 429 storm."
      ]
    },
    {
      "choice": "GET /{code} returns 404 with {\"error\":{\"code\":\"not_found\",...}} \u2014 byte-for-byte the same status, body and headers as a code that never existed. GET /api/links/{code}/stats, which the link's own owner uses, does report expired: true.",
      "decision": "What a request for an expired code returns",
      "rationale": "A visitor cannot use the redirect endpoint to learn that some code was once real, so a scraper cannot separate 'not yet issued' from 'issued and lapsed' and narrow its guessing space.",
      "rejected": [
        "410 Gone on expiry: confirms the code existed, turning the redirect endpoin

ACCEPTANCE CRITERIA
- With SHORTENER_API_KEYS="alpha:100,beta:20", LINKS_RATE_LIMIT_MAX=10 and the limiter enabled, 100 consecutive POST /api/links requests carrying header X-API-Key: alpha from one client address all return 201, and the 101st within the same 60 second window returns 429.
- With the same configuration, 20 POST /api/links requests carrying X-API-Key: beta return 201 and the 21st returns 429, proving each key uses its own quota value.
- A 429 produced by the per-key limiter has body {"error":{"code":"rate_limited","message":...}}, a Retry-After header whose value parses as an integer >= 1 and <= 60, and adds no row to the links table.
- After key alpha (quota 100) has been exhausted from client address A, the first POST /api/links carrying X-API-Key: beta from the same address A returns 201: buckets are keyed by API key, not by address, for known keys.
- After 15 successful POST /api/links requests carrying X-API-Key: alpha from client address A, a POST /api/links from address A with no X-API-Key header returns 201, showing key-limited requests never consumed the per-IP creation budget.
- With SHORTENER_API_KEYS unset or empty, POST /api/links behaviour is identical to today: the 11th creation from one address within the window returns 429 with Retry-After and the existing tests/test_rate_limit.py suite passes unchanged.
- A POST /api/links carrying X-API-Key: gamma (a name absent from SHORTENER_API_KEYS) is counted in the same per-IP creation bucket as key-less requests: 10 key-less creations followed by one gamma-keyed creation from the same address returns 429 for the gamma request.
- 1000 POST /api/links requests from one address each carrying a distinct random X-API-Key value produce the same per-IP throttling as 1000 key-less requests and create no additional limiter buckets beyond the per-IP one.
- GET /{code} requests carrying X-API-Key: alpha where alpha's quota is 1 still succeed with 307 for at least five consecutive visits: redirects are never limited by key and remain on the existing per-IP redirect bucket (LINKS_RATE_LIMIT_MAX * 100).
- GET /api/links/{code}/stats and GET /health are unaffected by X-API-Key: presence of any key value changes neither status code nor headers for these routes.
- With LINKS_RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false and SHORTENER_API_KEYS="alpha:2", 15 POST /api/links requests carrying X-API-Key: alpha all return 201.
- SHORTENER_API_KEYS=" alpha : 100 , beta:20 ," parses to exactly the two quotas 100 and 20 (surrounding whitespace and empty trailing entries tolerated).
- SHORTENER_API_KEYS="alpha:abc,noquota,:5,beta:0,gamma:7" causes the malformed entries to be discarded while gamma:7 is enforced; the service starts normally and requests with X-API-Key: alpha are treated as unknown (per-IP limit).
- Running the whole flow with a key value of "s3cret-alpha" leaves that string absent from the sqlite database files on disk and from captured log output at DEBUG level.
- PRAGMA table_info(links) and PRAGMA table_info(clicks) return the same columns as before the change and no new table exists in the database after exercising the key limiter.
- A per-key 429 is emitted by the ASGI middleware before request body parsing and before any database connection is opened for that request (no links row, no clicks row, and the response is produced even when the JSON body is malformed).
- Retry-After on a per-key 429 equals the whole number of seconds, rounded up and at least 1, until the oldest recorded hit for that key leaves the 60 second window.

CONSTRAINTS
- Python with FastAPI 0.115.6 / Starlette 0.41.3 / pydantic 2.10.4 as pinned in requirements.txt; no new runtime dependency may be added.
- Enforcement must remain in the existing ASGI middleware (app/ratelimit.py RateLimitMiddleware), running before routing, body parsing and any database access.
- No SQLite schema change: no new tables, columns or indexes; SCHEMA_STATEMENTS must stay as-is.
- No new HTTP endpoint and no admin surface; keys are read only from the process environment variable named exactly SHORTENER_API_KEYS.
- Keys are presented in the X-API-Key request header (HTTP header name matching is case-insensitive; the value is compared exactly, case-sensitively).
- Per-key limiting applies only to POST /api/links; GET /{code} redirect throttling, its multiplier and its per-IP keying must remain byte-for-byte behaviourally identical.
- Requests with no key or an unrecognised key must retain today's per-IP creation limit exactly, including the existing LINKS_RATE_LIMIT_MAX, window, Retry-After and error envelope.
- All 429 responses keep the existing envelope {"error":{"code":"rate_limited","message":...}} with Cache-Control: no-store and Retry-After in whole seconds >= 1.
- API keys are credentials: the key value must never be written to the database, to a file, to a log record or to any response body, and limiter state must key on a per-boot salted hash of the key, mirroring the existing treatment of client addresses.
- Key comparison and lookup must not leak whether a key exists through the response: an unknown key yields the same status and body shape as no key at all (no 401/403 path is introduced).
- Unknown or attacker-supplied key values must not be able to grow limiter memory: such requests fall back to the per-IP bucket, and the existing MAX_TRACKED_KEYS bound on tracked buckets must continue to hold.
- Invalid configuration must fail soft in the style of app/config.py: a malformed SHORTENER_API_KEYS entry is logged (without the key value) and skipped rather than raising at startup.
- Existing environment variable names, defaults and documented behaviour remain unchanged; the change is purely additive.
- The existing test suite under tests/ must continue to pass without modification.
- Limiter state stays in-process and non-persistent, thread-safe under the existing threading.Lock, and vanishes on restart.

Implement this design as a complete, runnable service. Include requirements.txt with pinned versions. The next stage generates tests against the files you return and reviews them line by line, so return the code you would defend in that review.
